# HTML

HTML Rendering for Documents: Transforming WYSIWYG and AI-Generated HTML into ODT, DOCX, and PDF.  
ENTERPRISE FEATURE Available for:  
✓ Carbone Cloud  
✓ Carbone On-premise  
✗ Embedded Carbone JS   v5.0+ 

## :html

> ℹ️ **Note:** Compatible with DOCX, ODT and HTML templates. The generated document can be exported to PDF.

The `:html` formatter converts HTML content into native document formatting for DOCX and ODT templates, enabling rich text, structured layouts, and semantic document elements. List of Supported HTML Elements:

| Category | Elements | Documentation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Text formatting** | `<b>`, `<strong>`, `<i>`, `<em>`, `<u>`, `<s>`, `<del>`, `<sup>`, `<sub>`, `<mark>`, `<code>`, `<kbd>`, `<samp>` | [Formatting Elements](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#formatting-elements) |
| **Structure** | `<p>`, `<br>`, `<pre>`, `<hr>` | [Structure Elements](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#structure-elements) |
| **Lists** | `<ul>`, `<ol>`, `<li>` | [List Elements](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#list-elements) |
| **Task lists** | `<input type="checkbox">` | [Checkbox Element](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#checkbox-element) |
| **Quotes** | `<blockquote>` | [Quote Element](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#quote-element) |
| **Headings** | `<h1>`,`<h2>`,`<h3>`,`<h4>`,`<h5>`, `<h6>` | [Heading Elements](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#heading-elements) |
| **Tables** | `<table>`, `<tr>`, `<th>`, `<td>` (with `colspan`, `rowspan`) | [Table Element](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#table-element) |
| **Links** | `<a href="...">` | [Anchor Element](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#hyperlink-element) |
| **Media** | `<img src="...">` | [Image Element](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#image-element) |

**Notes**

-   Tags and attributes not listed above are ignored during conversion. Their content is still rendered as unformatted text.

## Usage

```cdata
{
  "name" : "<b>raptor</b>",
  "description" : "The engine is <u>powered</u> by <i>cryogenic liquid methane</i><br>and<br><b><i>liquid oxygen</i></b> (LOX),<br><s>rather than the RP-1 kerosene and LOX</s>."
}
```

```ctemplate
Name:{d.name:html}

Description: {d.description:html}
```

```cresult
Name:
<b>raptor</b>

Description:
The engine is <u>powered</u> by <i>cryogenic liquid methane</i>
and
<b><i>liquid oxygen</i></b> (LOX),
<s>rather than the RP-1 kerosene and LOX</s>.
```

**Note:** The `:html` formatter renders the HTML content in a [new paragraph](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#paragraph-handling). To inject HTML in the current paragraph, enable the **inline** mode.

## Options

| Option | Description | Usage | Applies to |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `inline` | Render HTML within the current paragraph without creating new paragraphs or line breaks. [Learn more.](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#paragraph-handling) | `{d.value:html(inline)}` | `<a>`, `<b>`, `<strong>`, `<em>`, `<i>`, `<s>`, `<del>`, `<u>`, `<sup>`, `<sub>`, `<mark>`, `<code>`, `<kbd>`, `<samp>` |
| `nospace` | Remove automatic spacing after HTML block elements. [Learn more.](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#spacing-behaviors) | `{d.value:html(nospace)}` | `<p>`, `<h1>` - `<h6>`, `<ul>`, `<ol>`, `<table>`, `<pre>` |
| `headingtheme` | Apply custom heading styles using a theme prefix. [Learn More.](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#heading-elements) | `{d.value:html(headingtheme:custom-)}` | `<h1>` - `<h6>` |
| `tabletheme` | Apply custom table style (DOCX only). [Learn more.](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#table-element) | `{d.value:html(tabletheme:GridTable2)}` | `<table>` |
| `quotetheme` | Apply a paragraph style of the template to quotes, instead of the default indentation. [Learn more.](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#quote-element) | `{d.value:html(quotetheme:Quote)}` | `<blockquote>` |

**Note:** Options can be combined by separating them with commas, e.g., `{d.value:html(nospace,headingtheme:custom-)}`

## CSS Styles

The `:html` formatter supports inline CSS styling via the style attribute on HTML elements. A style applied to the Carbone tag takes priority over the same property defined in the HTML content, learn more on [Style Inheritance](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#style-inheritance).

**Example of inline style attributes**  

```html
<p style="color:green;background-color:#FF00FF"><b>OK</b></p> 
```

**Supported CSS Properties**  
Text and background colors:

-   `color`: Text color
-   `background-color`: Background color, except on `<mark>` which always renders a yellow highlight
-   **Note**: Additional CSS properties will be supported in future releases.

Page breaks ([Learn More](/documentation/design/advanced-features/html.md#page-breaks)):

-   `break-before="page"`: Insert a page break before the paragraph
-   `break-after="page"`: Insert a page break after the paragraph

**Not supported**  
External stylesheets, `<style>` elements, CSS classes, and IDs are ignored.

**Supported Color Formats**

| Format | Description | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Hexadecimal** | Six-digit hex notation (RGB) | `#FF00BB`, `#faebd7` |
| **RGB** | Red, green, blue values (0-255) | `rgb(31 120 50)`, `rgb(31,120,50)` |
| **HSL** | Hue, saturation, lightness | `hsl(120deg 75% 25%)`, `hsl(120 75 25)`, `hsl(120,75,25)` |
| **Named colors** | CSS color keywords | `red`, `blue`, `lightseagreen` ([full list](https://www.w3.org/wiki/CSS/Properties/color/keywords)) |

## Page Breaks

The `:html` formatter supports CSS page break properties to control pagination. Page break properties currently apply only to Paragraph Elements (`<p>`).

**Enabling Page Break Support**  

This is a beta feature since version [5.2.0](/changelog.md#v5-2-0). To enable this functionality, add the following pre-release tag to your template: `{o.preReleaseFeatureIn=5002000}`. Without this tag, page break styles are ignored.

**Example Usage**  

```html
<!-- Page break before paragraph -->
<p style="break-before: page;">This paragraph starts on a new page</p>

<!-- Page break after paragraph -->
<p style="break-after: page;">This paragraph ends the page</p>
```

## Style Inheritance

HTML content automatically inherits the styles applied to the Carbone tag, where it's inserted. For example, if you apply "Noto Sans" font at 20px to a Carbone tag, e.g. `{d.content:html}`, the injected HTML content will render using "Noto Sans" at "20px".

**Inherited styles**  

-   Font family and font size
-   Text color
-   Background color
-   Text alignment
-   Text direction (RTL)

**Priority**  

A style applied to the Carbone tag takes priority over the same property defined in the HTML content. If the tag does not define the property, the CSS provided in the HTML content applies, e.g. `<p style="color:green">`.

## Paragraph Handling

When the HTML tag is placed inside a paragraph and mixed with other content, the content will be pushed into a new paragraph above or below the rendered HTML, e.g. [HTML Usage](#usage). Use the **inline** mode, to inject the HTML inside a paragraph.

**Inline Option Example**  

```cdata
{
  "value" : "<b>The text is injected within the current paragraph</b>",
}
```

```ctemplate
After

Beginning - {d.value:html(inline)} - End

Before
```

```cresult
After

Beginning - <b>The text is injected within the current paragraph</b> - End

Before
```

## Spacing Behaviors

An empty paragraph is automatically injected after each paragraph, heading, list, table and preformatted block (`<pre>`). It mimics the bottom padding applied by default by web browsers on these elements. Use the **nospace** option to remove the empty paragraph, and therefore the space, e.g. `{d.content:html(nospace)}`.

**Nospace Option Example**  

```cdata
{
  "name" : 'Banana',
  "description" : '<p><b>is an elongated, edible fruit</b></p>'
}
```

```ctemplate
The famous fruit {d.name} {d.description:html(nospace)}, botanically a berry.
```

```cresult
The famous fruit Banana
<b>is an elongated, edible fruit</b>
, botanically a berry.
```

## Entities

The `:html` formatter supports the following entity formats:

-   **Named entities**: `&amp;`, `&copy;`, `&nbsp;`, etc.
-   **Decimal numeric entities**: `&#169;`, `&#128512;`
-   **Hexadecimal numeric entities**: `&#xA9;`, `&#x1F600;`

Emoji characters are supported as literal Unicode or as numeric entities.

## Tabs

Use the character entities `&ensp;` or `&emsp;` to create a tab. Avoid using `&#9;`, as HTML parsers will collapse it into a single space due to the whitespace collapse principle. To control tab spacing in text editors:

-   LibreOffice: Select the paragraph where the HTML formatter is > Right Click > Click on "Paragraph" > Paragraphs… > Click on the "Tabs" tab > Define a position value in inches > Save.
-   MS Word: Select the paragraph where the HTML formatter is > Right Click > Paragraph > Click on the "Tabs…" button at the bottom of the menu > Change the default stops or add a new tab stop > Save by clicking on "OK".

